Scenario: Create contact external link attempt as non permissioned user
	Koroneiki contact external links should not be created via API by non permissioned users.

	Given I create a contact on koroneiki with the following values
	| Email Address | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | Koroneiki                                |
	| Language      | English                                  |
	| Last Name     | Contact1                                 |
	| Middle Name   | User                                     |
	And I attempt to create an external link for the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" with the following values as a non permissioned user
	| Domain      | koroneikicontact |
	| Entity Id   | 1234             |
	| Entity Name | KoroneikiContact |
	Then the external link with the entity id "1234" should not be present on the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken"

Scenario: Create contact external link via okta id attempt as non permissioned user
	Koroneiki contact external links should not be created via okta id via API by non permissioned users.

	Given I create a contact on koroneiki with the following values
	| Email Address | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | Koroneiki                                |
	| Language      | English                                  |
	| Last Name     | Contact1                                 |
	| Middle Name   | User                                     |
	And I attempt to create an external link for the contact with the okta ID "koroneikicontact1" with the following values as a non permissioned user
	| Domain      | koroneikicontact |
	| Entity Id   | 1234             |
	| Entity Name | KoroneikiContact |
	Then the external link with the entity id "1234" should not be present on the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken"

Scenario: View contact external link attempt as non permissioned user
	Koroneiki contact external links should not be viewable via API by non permissioned users.

	Given I create a contact on koroneiki with the following values
	| Email Address | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | Koroneiki                                |
	| Language      | English                                  |
	| Last Name     | Contact1                                 |
	| Middle Name   | User                                     |
	And I create an external link for the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" with the following values
	| Domain      | koroneikicontact |
	| Entity Id   | 1234             |
	| Entity Name | KoroneikiContact |
	Then the external link with the entity id "1234" should be present on the contact with the okta ID "koroneikicontact1" with the following values
	| Domain      | koroneikicontact |
	| Entity Id   | 1234             |
	| Entity Name | KoroneikiContact |
	And the external link with the entity id "1234" on the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not be visible to a non permissioned user

Scenario: Remove contact external link attempt as non permissioned user
	Koroneiki contact external links should not be removable via API by non permissioned users.

	Given I create a contact on koroneiki with the following values
	| Email Address | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | Koroneiki                                |
	| Language      | English                                  |
	| Last Name     | Contact1                                 |
	| Middle Name   | User                                     |
	And I create an external link for the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" with the following values
	| Domain      | koroneikicontact |
	| Entity Id   | 1234             |
	| Entity Name | KoroneikiContact |
	And I attempt to delete an external link with the entity id "1234" on the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" as a non permissioned user
	Then the external link with the entity id "1234" should be present on the contact with the okta ID "koroneikicontact1" with the following values
	| Domain      | koroneikicontact |
	| Entity Id   | 1234             |
	| Entity Name | KoroneikiContact |
	And the external link with the entity id "1234" on the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not be visible to a non permissioned user

Scenario: Set contact permission attempt via uuid as non permissioned user
	Koroneiki contact permissions should not be able to be set via uuid via API by non permissioned users.

	Given I create a contact on koroneiki with the following values
	| Email Address | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | Koroneiki                                |
	| Language      | English                                  |
	| Last Name     | Contact1                                 |
	| Middle Name   | User                                     |
	And I attempt to set the permissions for a contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to have the following values for a non permissioned user as a non permissioned user
	| Update | true |
	| View   | true |
	And I attempt to update a koroneiki contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" via uuid to have the following values as a non permissioned user
	| Email Address | koroneiki.contact2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | Koroneiki                                |
	| Last Name     | Contact2                                 |
	| Middle Name   | User                                     |
	Then I should be able to view a koroneiki contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" and the following values
	| Email Address | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | Koroneiki                                |
	| Language      | English                                  |
	| Last Name     | Contact1                                 |
	| Middle Name   | User                                     |
	And I should not be able to view a koroneiki contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact2@lrcustomer.com.broken"
	And I should not be able to view a koroneiki contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" as a non permissioned user

Scenario: Set contact permission attempt via okta id as non permissioned user
	Koroneiki contact permissions should not be able to be set via okta id via API by non permissioned users.

	Given I create a contact on koroneiki with the following values
